Your `Context` is null, it would be better if you create a `Context` parameter in your `getInstance()` method instead of just storing it in your `CartDatabase` class  without instantiating it

> Try the following code

    public static CartDatabase getInstance(Context context) {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = Room.databaseBuilder(context, CartDatabase.class, "Cart")//if we want in memory builder  ithink we can add it here
                    .allowMainThreadQueries().build();
        }
        return instance;
    }


> Then on your `onClick()`

    CartDatabase.getInstance(getApplicationContext()).cartDAO().insertToCart(cart);

