Sug_Text:
Just use [*format*][1] from *date-fns* like that:

```javascript
format((seconds * 1000), 'mm:ss')
```

if there is a need to remove timezone hours offset as well, 
[*getTimezoneOffset* (in minutes)][2] can be used:

```javascript
let dt = new Date((seconds * 1000));
dt = addMinutes(dt, dt.getTimezoneOffset());
return format(dt, 'mm:ss');
```

  [1]: https://date-fns.org/v2.25.0/docs/format
  [2]: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/getTimezoneOffset

