Sug_Text:
I did a proof of concept with some modifications from what you originally had. See below,

**DEMO:** http://jsfiddle.net/esu7A/2/

    $(function() {
        $('div').focus();
        var x = ['SELECT', 'WHERE', 'FROM'];
        $('div').keyup(function(e) {
            //console.log(e.keyCode) ;
            if (e.keyCode == 32) {
                $('div').html(function(i, v) { 
                    $.each(x, function(i, xv) {
                        var sRegx = new RegExp(xv, "gi");

                        v = v.replace(sRegx, function(key) {                     
                            return '<span style="color: blue; text-transform: 
                           uppercase;">' + key + '</span>';
                        });
                    });                               
                    return v;
                });
            }
        });

    });

You going to extend this further to handle

1. Backspace
2. HTML contents from previous inserts
3. Cursor position

and more..

