As the [showcase explains][1], there's no need of manually passing the current selected event as an argument to the listener method. Just declare a method where you catch the incoming event and get the data from it. After that, you can call your redirect method with everything you need.

<!-- language: lang-xml -->

    <p:ajax event="eventSelect"  
            listener="#{LeadListController.onEventSelect}" />

<!-- language: lang-java -->

    public void onEventSelect(SelectEvent selectEvent) {  
        ScheduleEvent event = (ScheduleEvent) selectEvent.getObject();  
        redirect(event.getData());
    }  

Appart from that and totally unrelated to the problem, I encourage you to name your managed beans as the bean class name with the first letter lowercased. It's a java specification that has been already discussed [here][2].


  [1]: http://www.primefaces.org/showcase/ui/schedule.jsf
  [2]: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/12297006/java-class-name-convention-with-respect-to-managed-been-usage-in-primefaces

