Sug_Text:
.jar files aren't executable by themselves, they are executed by java.exe, and only if the MANIFEST.MF file (in the special META-INF folder) states a Main-Class:

>Manifest-Version: 1.0 <br>
>**Main-Class: com.test.Test**



    package com.test;

    public class Test
    {
      public static void main(String[] args)
      {
        System.out.println("Hello from Test");
      }
    }

Use the Process class and it's methods if you want to execute jar files

    public class Exec
    {
       public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception
       {
            Process ps = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(new String[]{System.getProperty("java.home"), "-jar", "Test.jar"});
            ps.waitFor();
            java.io.InputStream is = ps.getInputStream();
            byte b[] = new byte[is.available()];
            is.read(b, 0, b.length);
            System.out.println(new String(b));
        }
    }
System.getProperty("java.home") returns the location of the current JRE if you're wondering, and is recommended (by me) over just writing 'java' because java is only added to the path by default if you install the JDK.

